{
  "file": "Guidance for national",
  "page": 59,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "bbox": [
        36.0,
        21.884788513183594,
        63.09400177001953,
        32.93328857421875
      ],
      "text": "Second",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightCn",
      "size": 9.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        63.09400177001953,
        21.884788513183594,
        86.86299896240234,
        32.93328857421875
      ],
      "text": "edition",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightCn",
      "size": 9.5,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        84.28973388671875,
        513.4489135742188,
        97.6412353515625
      ],
      "text": "and pericardial TB. Corticosteroids have been shown to improve survival and reduce",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        100.2862548828125,
        513.4605712890625,
        113.63775634765625
      ],
      "text": "morbidity in advanced tuberculous meningitis and are thus recommended in all cases",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        116.21377563476562,
        513.3799438476562,
        129.63427734375
      ],
      "text": "(10) of tuberculous meningitis  . Prednisone is used most frequently, in a dosage of",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightItali",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        132.279296875,
        513.3916015625,
        145.63079833984375
      ],
      "text": "2 mg/kg daily, increased to 4 mg/kg daily in the case of the most seriously ill children,",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        148.27581787109375,
        513.4833984375,
        161.6273193359375
      ],
      "text": "with a maximum dosage of 60 mg/day for 4 weeks. The dose should then be gradually",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        164.2723388671875,
        291.6829528808594,
        177.62384033203125
      ],
      "text": "reduced over 1–2 weeks before stopping.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        188.70986938476562,
        220.49786376953125,
        202.13037109375
      ],
      "text": "Pyridoxine supplementation",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightItali",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        213.28533935546875,
        513.46044921875,
        226.6368408203125
      ],
      "text": "Isoniazid may cause symptomatic pyridoxine deficiency, which presents as neuropathy,",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        229.2818603515625,
        513.41455078125,
        242.63336181640625
      ],
      "text": "particularly in severely malnourished children and HIV-positive children on antiretroviral",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        245.27838134765625,
        513.4489135742188,
        258.6298828125
      ],
      "text": "therapy (ART). Supplemental pyridoxine (5–10 mg/day) is recommended in HIV-positive",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        261.2059020996094,
        327.4593200683594,
        274.62640380859375
      ],
      "text": "(7) or malnourished children being treated for TB  .",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightItali",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        285.7124328613281,
        177.6948699951172,
        299.1329345703125
      ],
      "text": "Nutritional support",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightItali",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        310.28790283203125,
        513.4028930664062,
        323.639404296875
      ],
      "text": "Severe malnutrition is associated with increased mortality in TB patients - children and",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        326.2843933105469,
        513.4146118164062,
        339.6358947753906
      ],
      "text": "adults - and a child’s nutritional status should be assessed regularly during treatment of TB.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        342.2808837890625,
        513.3798828125,
        355.63238525390625
      ],
      "text": "All children diagnosed with TB who do not need treatment for severe acute malnutrition",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        358.2773742675781,
        513.3798828125,
        371.6288757324219
      ],
      "text": "require nutritional support. This includes early efforts to continue breastfeeding (until at",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        374.27386474609375,
        513.4605102539062,
        387.6253662109375
      ],
      "text": "least 24 months of age where possible) and to ensure adequate nutrient intake on the",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        390.2703552246094,
        513.4375610351562,
        403.6218566894531
      ],
      "text": "basis of locally available and affordable foods. Additional energy is particularly important",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        406.266845703125,
        513.3800659179688,
        419.61834716796875
      ],
      "text": "during the intensive phase of treatment and is best given through additional household",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        422.2633361816406,
        513.3685913085938,
        435.6148376464844
      ],
      "text": "foods, provided as part of a balanced varied diet. Infants under 6 months of age causing",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        438.25982666015625,
        513.4028930664062,
        451.611328125
      ],
      "text": "concern about malnutrition or growth failure require referral to a therapeutic feeding",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        454.2563171386719,
        513.4721069335938,
        467.6078186035156
      ],
      "text": "programme. If this is not available or feasible, breastfeeding mothers should be given",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        470.2528076171875,
        513.4144897460938,
        483.60430908203125
      ],
      "text": "support to optimize breastfeeding. Nutritional supplementation cannot be given directly",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        486.1802978515625,
        510.29791259765625,
        499.6007995605469
      ],
      "text": "(11- to an infant under 6 months of age but can be provided for the lactating mother",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightItali",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        502.1767883300781,
        104.22138977050781,
        515.5972900390625
      ],
      "text": "17) .",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightItali",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        529.4659423828125,
        263.7552795410156,
        543.6859130859375
      ],
      "text": "Management of adverse events",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-BoldItalic",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        552.2094116210938,
        513.4833984375,
        565.5609130859375
      ],
      "text": "Adverse events caused by anti-TB drugs are much less common in children than in adults",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        568.1369018554688,
        513.3683471679688,
        581.557373046875
      ],
      "text": "(9) . The most important adverse event is the development of hepatotoxicity, which can be",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightItali",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        584.202392578125,
        513.391357421875,
        597.5538940429688
      ],
      "text": "caused by isoniazid, rifampicin or pyrazinamide. Serum liver enzyme levels do not need",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        600.1989135742188,
        513.4718627929688,
        613.5504150390625
      ],
      "text": "to be monitored routinely, as asymptomatic mild elevation of serum liver enzymes (less",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        616.1954345703125,
        513.4258422851562,
        629.5469360351562
      ],
      "text": "than five times the normal values) is not an indication to stop treatment. However, the",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        632.1919555664062,
        513.4375,
        645.54345703125
      ],
      "text": "occurrence of liver tenderness, hepatomegaly or jaundice should prompt investigation",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        648.1884155273438,
        513.4144897460938,
        661.5399169921875
      ],
      "text": "of serum liver enzyme levels and the immediate stopping of all potentially hepatotoxic",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        664.1849365234375,
        513.3914794921875,
        677.5364379882812
      ],
      "text": "drugs. Patients should be screened for other causes of hepatitis, and no attempt should",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        680.1814575195312,
        513.4718017578125,
        693.532958984375
      ],
      "text": "be made to reintroduce these drugs until liver functions have normalized. An expert",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        696.1779174804688,
        513.4144287109375,
        709.5294189453125
      ],
      "text": "with experience in managing drug-induced hepatotoxicity should be involved in the",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        712.1744384765625,
        513.414306640625,
        725.5259399414062
      ],
      "text": "further management of such cases. Early signs of ethambutol toxicity can be tested in",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        728.1709594726562,
        513.4720458984375,
        741.5224609375
      ],
      "text": "the older child through red-green colour discrimination. Monitoring for optic neuritis",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        744.1674194335938,
        274.6282653808594,
        757.5189208984375
      ],
      "text": "can be sought early when appropriate.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        14.202799797058105,
        805.8439331054688,
        36.44280242919922,
        835.8439331054688
      ],
      "text": "40",
      "font": "HelveticaNeue-Light",
      "size": 20.0,
      "type": "heading_main"
    }
  ]
}